 "final_text": "## Summary for Sam\n\n**Yes, Meadow Analytics was invoiced** \u2014 but the invoice never made it into the ERP or Books system, which is why they weren't findable there.\n\n- **Invoice:** INV-2026-047, $18,750.00 for \"Executive AI workshop \u2014 February program,\" sent 2026-02-06, Net 30 terms (due 2026-03-08)\n- **Why they're missing from the ERP/Books:** Your own 2026-02-06 email notes Meadow Analytics' vendor/customer master-data setup in D365 was still pending (new client), so AR sent the invoice directly by email and tracked it in a manual tracker as a workaround \u2014 the customer entity was never actually created in either system. I confirmed zero matches for \"Meadow\" across Customers, Vendors, Sales Orders, and CustomerTransactions in the ERP, and zero matches in Books' Customer/Invoice tables.\n- **Payment status:** Meadow Analytics' AP team confirmed receipt on 2026-02-24 and said it was queued in their March payment run \u2014 but there's no payment/remittance confirmation anywhere in email, ERP, or Books. Since it's now August (5+ months past the 3/8 due date) with no proof of payment, the full **$18,750 should be treated as outstanding**.\n\nRecommend: get Meadow Analytics' customer entity created in D365/Books now, load INV-2026-047 into it, and follow up on payment status directly \u2014 this invoice has effectively been \"off the books\" since February.",
